X:1
T:Si So, Gorniog
T:See-Saw, Swaddled One
R:cân
S:https://amgueddfa.cymru/casgliadau/caneuongwerin/?id=9 (collected by D. Roy Saer)
N:Sung by Llew Evans (born 1890), a farmer, of Ystumgwadneth, Rhyd-y-main, near Dolgellau, Meirionnydd; recorded 18.4.63 (St Fagans tape 315). A rocking song his mother sang to him at the Ystumgwadneth hearth when he was a little boy. The three pence in verse 1 seem to be payment for sawing; there may be a link between English "See-saw" rhymes and the singing of sawyers at work, and sawing turns up in several Welsh nursery rhymes ("Llifio, llifio, coed Llandeilo").
N:The second C in bar 3 ("en-nill") is in brackets on the score.
